# Vendored terminal emulator

The files in this directory are not written by this project. They come from
[termux/termux-app](https://github.com/termux/termux-app), module
`terminal-emulator`, at `master` as fetched on 2026-10-23.

## License

Apache License 2.0. This is not an assumption: termux-app's own `LICENSE.md`
states it explicitly.

> The `termux/termux-app` repository is released under GPLv3 only license.
>
> ### Exceptions
>
> - Terminal Emulator for Android code is used which is released under
>   Apache 2.0 license. Check `terminal-view` and `terminal-emulator` libraries.

The rest of termux-app (including `jni/termux.c`, the app module) is GPLv3 and
is **not** used here. The pty binding this project ships is
`android/jni/pty.c`, written from scratch against the POSIX `forkpty` API.

`terminal-view` is deliberately not vendored: it depends on the annotation and support libraries and on
Gradle-resolved AARs, while this APK is assembled by `android/assemble-apk.sh`
with plain `javac` + `d8`. The renderer is `io.opencrabs.mobile.TerminalPane`
instead.

A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

## Files and modifications

Vendored unchanged:

- `AndroidUtils.java`
- `ByteQueue.java`
- `ITermImage.java`
- `KeyHandler.java`
- `Logger.java`
- `TerminalBitmap.java`
- `TerminalBuffer.java`
- `TerminalColorScheme.java`
- `TerminalColors.java`
- `TerminalEmulator.java`
- `TerminalOutput.java`
- `TerminalRow.java`
- `TerminalSession.java`
- `TerminalSixel.java`
- `TextStyle.java`
- `WcWidth.java`

Modified, each with a `MODIFIED for OpenCrabs` note in its own header:

- `TerminalSessionClient.java` - `@NonNull` and `@Nullable` annotations from the annotation library
  removed. They are compile-time hints with CLASS retention, and they are the
  only external annotation reference in the module. Keeping them would force the hand-rolled
  build to unpack an AAR for no runtime effect.
- `JNI.java` - no longer a `System.loadLibrary("termux")` binding, because that
  library's source is GPLv3. Method signatures are unchanged so every other
  vendored file compiles as-is; the bodies forward to `io.opencrabs.mobile.Pty`.
